{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/771332-earthbound-fae","id":771332,"title":"Earthbound & Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-22T01:57:52-08:00","id":771332,"title":"Earthbound & Fae","content":"Hello everyone. I would like to ask a question about how should be the interaction between an Earthbound &amp; Fae.<br /> <br /> First of all, I use the term Fae because I would like to know before and after the shattering, so using the term Changeling could have been insufficient. We all know that generally Earthbounds are grotesque creatures. I want to know that if Fae could be grotesque as Earthbound or they scared as hell when they see one. Also, if Fae are far a part from Earthbounds can us think some Fomorians as grotesque.<br /> <br /> The thing is that, I want to use a contract between 9 Fae and a Earthbound to defeat another Earthbound. I don't want to miss a point while directing that game. Therefore, I need to be sure that my team can handle the scene or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T06:14:26-08:00","id":771438,"title":"","content":"Unseelie fae might get involved with an Earthbound, but I imagine most fae would consider them to be either Fomorians or allied with Fomorians. Fae see other supernaturals as misguided or corrupted fae, so that would make sense.<br /> <br /> How the Earthbound see the fae, however, might be where it really gets interesting. Fae (especially in the DA setting) are generative beings of the Wyld. They form things from the Mists. However, the Elohim are also creators--albeit it, ones who seem more aligned with the Weaver than the Wyld. Would the Earthbound therefore recognise them as a kind of lesser angel, or would they see them as a random factor in the cosmos, disrupting the order of the Elohim? Would this make the Earthbound pleased, or jealous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:46:45-08:00","id":771627,"title":"","content":"Depending on how you read Demon, the Earthbound could remember the origin of the Fae and know to some degree what it is working with.<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't think it would judge the Fae as angels or care about their creative powers. The Earthbound are crazy by one side, and pretty practical by other. It will use the Changelings while trying to figure out any danger they can pose to its own agenda and wellbeing, and then do whatever suits it more. They barely recognize themselves as Elohim anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T20:06:30-08:00","id":772023,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages Fae are generally unafraid of other supernaturals. They consider themselves to be (and pretty much are) the top of the supernatural food chain. Not sure about the opinions of the Earthbound though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T20:34:00-08:00","id":772039,"title":"","content":"Mythology has a tradition of faeries (or their queen at any rate) owing a tithe to Hell. If that is reflected in the game, I suspect the Fae attitude toward the Earthbound would be much like Eastern Europeans' attitudes toward the Ottoman Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:38:54-08:00","id":772119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/771332-earthbound-fae?p=772039#post772039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mythology has a tradition of faeries (or their queen at any rate) owing a tithe to Hell. If that is reflected in the game, I suspect the Fae attitude toward the Earthbound would be much like Eastern Europeans' attitudes toward the Ottoman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only so because of Christians wanting to blame everyone and their mythologies into going into the light, so it's hardly applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:13:02-08:00","id":772600,"title":"","content":"The book Devil's Due has a sidebar on how the demons, Not nessesarily the earthbound but demons in general view the various supernatural types. Its been a while sense I read it and don't have it handy but as I remember Mages, ya we taught them how to do that they just dont remember. Shapeshifters (werewolves and changing breeds), ya we created them. Vampires, we created them too, human hunter types like inqueisitors, they use powers heaven gave them so we made them. So it was pretty much a big list of we where involved in creating everything and everyone because....ya we came first and we made everything cause we said so.<br /> <br /> Then it go to the Fae and the reaction was something like &quot;What the hell is that!, where did it come from, it was always here but I don't remember it ever existing but its here I am so confused&quot; so it looks like the two have nothing to do with eachother so little in fact that fallen angels who remember the world before it existed have no clue what they are or where they came from just that somehow they exist and that's just not right.<br /> <br /> The Fae for there part basically think of things from there point of view, so its sorta a consentual reality thing both sides see themselves as the first beings to exist and both remember the other groups showing up but as far as I know the Fae remember when Angels and demons first started appearing but the demons dont. Heck some Fae reinvent themselves as angelic or godly beings to draw power form human worship, some think that's lowering themselves.<br /> <br /> So ya though individual Fae might make pacts with demons for one reason or another as a whole they are not connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:48:32-08:00","id":776359,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2939_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2939\" data-vbnamecard=\"2939\">Avaron</a> The fae may be remembering when lucifer summoned the earthbound, but as far as the consensual reality thing there was a theory based on a old mage 1st edition sidebar. The sidebar stated that there may be other complete realities surrounding the individual spheres the same way there is a spirit realm for spirit, like parallel timelines and theoretical pasts/futures for time, 2 -dimensional and 5 -dimensional universes for correspondence, dream and concept realities for mind, etc.<br /> <br /> So the theory was that maybe just as there were multiple &quot;creations&quot; built in completely different ways and originally fully independent of each other, but when all of them turned out to be imperfect god scrapped them and moved on. so in order to stay &quot;existing&quot; they all just bled into each other and split apart into many &quot;theoretical&quot; realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-29-2015, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}